      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. But the part about \"unaided memory\" is what's worrying me. It feels a bit vague. Does that mean if I write a similar algorithm for another client next month, it's fine as long as I didn't copy-paste their actual files? Or could they argue I'm using their \"confidential information\" if the logic is too similar?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
