      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your interpretation is generally correct; the \"unaided memory\" clause typically permits the recall of general concepts, skills, or ideas that are naturally absorbed by a person. If you independently design a similar algorithm without copying their source code, you are likely safe under this clause. However, if the logic is so unique or closely matches their proprietary implementation that it strongly suggests derivation, they could potentially argue against it, making careful documentation of your independent creation advisable.",
      "source": "target",
